  'planned-water-shutdowns-plumstead-steenberg-cbd-2026-11-06',
  'Planned water shutdowns across Cape Town from 9 to 14 November',
  'Utilities', '2026-11-06', 'City of Cape Town', 'https://www.capetown.gov.za/media-and-news/planned-water-supply-maintenance-from-9-to-14-november/',
  'The City has scheduled water shutdowns in Plumstead, Steenberg, Lotus River, Hanover Park and the CBD between 9 and 14 November for pipeline and valve work.',
  'The City of Cape Town has announced scheduled work on its water network between 9 and 14 November. Most of the work involves connecting new pipelines or installing valves, and supply will be switched off in the affected areas while it is done.

On Monday 9 November, Plumstead streets including Woodgate, Southfield, Severn, Basil and Medway roads lose supply from 09:00 to 19:30. On Tuesday 10 November the City lists several shutdowns: more Plumstead roads (09:00 to 19:30), Loevenstein and Hoheizen (09:00 to 19:00), Lotus River (09:00 to 18:00), parts of Bantry Bay (09:00 to 18:00), Hanover Park and nearby areas (09:00 to 18:00), Elsies River (09:00 to 17:00) and Steenberg (08:00 to 20:00). Tankers are to be provided in Hanover Park and Elsies River.

On Wednesday 11 November, the Cape Town CBD around Buitengracht Street will be without water from 09:00 to 18:30 for a new meter connection. On Thursday 12 November, a Plumstead area bounded by Morton, Tiverton, Exeter, Thornbury and Hemyock roads is off from 09:00 to 19:30, and Steenberg is off again from 08:00 to 20:00. Kenwyn, Rondebosch East, parts of Lansdowne, Rylands and neighbouring areas will have lower than usual pressure from 09:00 to 17:00 while a main is shut, with the final connection expected by 18:00 on Saturday 14 November.

The City also plans zero-pressure tests between 09:00 and 16:00 on 10, 11 and 12 November in areas such as Diep River, Wynberg, Tamboerskloof and Gardens, where residents may see low pressure or no water. Crews will also check for leaks in Welgelegen, Table View, Tokai and Zevenwacht, which should not cut supply there. The City says water may look milky briefly after it returns and clears if left to stand. Updates are posted on the @CityofCTAlerts account on X.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.capetown.gov.za/media-and-news/planned-water-supply-maintenance-from-9-to-14-november/", "https://weekendargus.co.za/capetimes/2026-11-08-cape-town-water-disruptions-full-list-of-affected-areas-from-9-to-14-november/"]',
  'agent'
);
